      "dates_text": "Sunday 1 November 2026 - Sunday 28 March 2027",
      "description": "Book a free community group tour of Earthly Paradise: Radical Living in the UK Earthly Paradise: Radical Living in the UK explores the people and places that have shaped art and activism across Britain over the last 200 years. Through painting, drawing, photography, sound, objects and archival material, Earthly Paradise highlights individuals and communities who challenged social conventions and created new ways of living, working and imagining society. We are welcoming local community groups, faith groups and charities for free tours of the exhibition: From November 2026 to March 2027 Available on Mondays when the Gallery is closed to the public Group sizes: Minimum 10 people and maximum 20 people FREE of charge NOTE: These tours are being organised specifically for existing groups and organisations within the community. As tour spaces are limited, we prioritise local not-for-profit and charitable organisations only. If you are an individual or a group of friends wishing to attend a free tour, please check our What’s On for the next ‘Introduction to Earthly Paradise’, which take place each month during the show’s run. These are also free of charge and do not require a booking. Image: Exhibition install photograph by Graham Pearson for William Morris Gallery",
